exports[`ocd setup > from a checkout, turns on self-update and points everything at the install 1`] = `
"
Prerequisites
  ✓ Node 24.21.0
  ✓ git /bin/git
  ✓ OpenCode /bin/opencode
  ✓ OpenCode service running
  – Claude Code: not installed (optional)
  – Codex: not installed (optional)
  – GitHub CLI (pull requests): not installed (optional)
  – tmux: not installed (optional)

Configuration
  → wrote ~/.ocd/ocd.jsonc
  ✓ ~/.ocd/ocd.jsonc: manager ~/ocd-manager, 1 repo, 1 profile

Install
  → turned on selfUpdate (following <root>/ocd)
  → building OCD into ~/.ocd/install (a few minutes)…
  ✓ installed abc1234; OCD runs from the install from now on

Manager
  → created ~/ocd-manager
  → ~/ocd-manager/.opencode/opencode.jsonc loads ~/.ocd/install/current/packages/plugin
  → wrote ~/ocd-manager/AGENTS.md

Command
  → ~/.local/bin/ocd → ~/.ocd/install/current/packages/cli/dist/ocd.mjs

Background service
  → background service installed

OpenCode
  → reloaded OpenCode, so the manager picks up the plugin

Notifications
  ✓ test notification sent

Check (ocd doctor)

Done
  Open OpenCode in the manager directory and ask it for work:
    cd ~/ocd-manager && opencode
    "In my-app, fix …"
  More repositories: \`ocd repo add <name> <path>\`. Profiles and settings: ocd.jsonc.
  Run \`ocd setup\` again any time to check or repair this setup.

asked:
No config at ~/.ocd/ocd.jsonc. Create one, or link an existing file (for example in a config repo)?
Manager directory (OpenCode sessions started there act as the OCD manager)
Model for OpenCode workers (provider/model)
Let the manager dispatch work to ~/code/my-app (as "my-app")?
Another repository the manager may work in (path, empty to finish)
Keep OCD up to date from <root>/ocd? New commits on its default branch are built into ~/.ocd/install, smoke-tested and switched to (selfUpdate)
Create the manager directory ~/ocd-manager?
Set up ~/ocd-manager/.opencode/opencode.jsonc to load the OCD plugin from ~/.ocd/install/current/packages/plugin?
Write starter instructions for the manager (AGENTS.md)?
Put \`ocd\` on your PATH: link ~/.local/bin/ocd → ~/.ocd/install/current/packages/cli/dist/ocd.mjs?
Install the background service? The supervisor then runs in the background and starts at login

ran:
